From ef6556ba6df7946c8b4cf1b0d5f95439822547da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:47:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] shared: isValidMacAddress() refuses any character but hex
 digits and separators (102.8 line)

Port of 0ed63f725be. Stock set s = -1 on any other character and went on,
so a separator after one hex digit (i / 2 - 1 == -1) put the count back and
A":A:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF passed. On this line the AiMesh gates in web.c already
run reaper_mac_or_empty()'s character whitelist first, but other callers
take isValidMacAddress() alone (the user-icon MAC has no length check), so
the function itself is hardened here too, as on the 102.10 line.

(cherry picked from commit 0ed63f725be, shared/misc.c only)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/shared/misc.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/shared/misc.c b/release/src/router/shared/misc.c
index 01e3d8afc21..9fcdf42e774 100644
--- a/release/src/router/shared/misc.c
+++ b/release/src/router/shared/misc.c
@@ -6026,7 +6026,11 @@ int isValidMacAddress(const char* mac) {
 			++s;
 		}
 		else
-			s = -1;
+			/* Reaper 2026-10-27: any other character makes it no MAC. Stock set s = -1 and went
+			 * on, so a separator after one hex digit (i / 2 - 1 == -1) put the count back and
+			 * A":A:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF passed - a quote or brace into the JSON events httpd writes
+			 * for cfg_server from re_mac / new_re_mac / target_bssid. */
+			return 0;
 		++mac;
 	}
 	return (i == 12 && (s == 5 || s == 0));
-- 
